It is also possible to configure new trusts. For example, we can add the Red Hat public GPG key
to check the signature of UBI images.
First, we need to download the Red Hat public key:
$ sudo wget -O /etc/pki/rpm-gpg/RPM-GPG-KEY-redhat \
https://www.redhat.com/security/data/fd431d51.txt
After idx_7f19a49a downloading the key, we must configure idx_dbd1f214 the image trust for UBI 9 images that have been
pulled from registry.access.redhat.com using the podman image trust set command:
$ sudo podman image trust set -f /etc/pki/rpm-gpg/RPM-GPG-KEY-redhat
registry.access.redhat.com/ubi9
